IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cra-types`
IMPORT `cra-goods`
IMPORT `cra-services`

-- Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK) — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "The goods (or services) do not conform. Until when can the consumer
--    reject them in the short term; is the fault presumed to have existed on
--    delivery; are the tier-two remedies open, what refund is due and by
--    when; and for services, repeat performance or a price reduction?"

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Consumer case` HAS
    `the goods`                                         IS A MAYBE `Goods supply`
    `a repair or replacement`                           IS A MAYBE `Repair or replacement`
    `the fault`                                         IS A MAYBE `Fault facts`
    `tier two`                                          IS A MAYBE `Tier two facts`
    `the service`                                       IS A MAYBE `Service facts`

DECLARE `Consumer position` HAS
    `last day for the short-term right to reject`       IS A MAYBE DATE
    `presumed not to conform on delivery`               IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `tier-two remedies available`                       IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `refund on final rejection`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `last day for the goods refund`                     IS A MAYBE DATE
    `repeat performance can be required`                IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `service price reduction available`                 IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `last day for the service refund`                   IS A MAYBE DATE

@ref ss 19-24, 54-56
@export default The position under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 (UK) when goods or services do not conform: the last day for the short-term right to reject (s 22); whether the fault is presumed to have existed on delivery (s 19(14)); whether the final right to reject or a price reduction is available (s 24(5)), the refund on final rejection with any deduction for use (s 24(8)-(10)) and the last day to pay it (s 20(15)); and for services, whether repeat performance can be required (s 55), whether a price reduction is available (s 56(3)), and the last day for its refund (s 56(4)). Each is NOTHING where its facts are not given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Consumer case`  @desc The goods and their dates, any repair or replacement, the fault, the tier-two facts, and any service
GIVETH A `Consumer position`
`the consumer position for` c MEANS
    `Consumer position` WITH
        `last day for the short-term right to reject`   IS
            CONSIDER c's `the goods`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST g  THEN JUST (`the last day for the short-term right to reject for` g `with` (c's `a repair or replacement`))
        `presumed not to conform on delivery`           IS
            CONSIDER c's `the goods`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST g  THEN
                CONSIDER c's `the fault`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST f  THEN JUST (`the goods are presumed not to have conformed on delivery for` g `with` f)
        `tier-two remedies available`                   IS
            CONSIDER c's `tier two`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the tier-two remedies are available under` t)
        `refund on final rejection`                     IS
            CONSIDER c's `the goods`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST g  THEN
                CONSIDER c's `tier two`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                WHEN JUST t  THEN JUST (`the refund on final rejection for` g `with` t)
        `last day for the goods refund`                 IS
            CONSIDER c's `tier two`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST t  THEN
                IF `the tier-two remedies are available under` t
                THEN JUST (`the last day for a refund agreed on` (t's `trader agreed to refund on`))
                ELSE NOTHING
        `repeat performance can be required`            IS
            CONSIDER c's `the service`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`repeat performance can be required for` s)
        `service price reduction available`             IS
            CONSIDER c's `the service`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN JUST (`a price reduction is available for` s)
        `last day for the service refund`               IS
            CONSIDER c's `the service`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST s  THEN
                IF `a price reduction is available for` s
                THEN CONSIDER s's `trader agreed to refund on`
                     WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                     WHEN JUST a  THEN JUST (`the last day for a refund agreed on` a)
                ELSE NOTHING
